      "$36 - 4k > 0 \\Rightarrow 36 > 4k$.",
      "$k < 9$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "\u5c0d\u65bc\u5169\u500b\u4e0d\u76f8\u7b49\u7684\u5be6\u6839\uff0c$\\Delta > 0$\u3002",
      "$6^2 - 4(1)(k) > 0$\u3002",
      "$36 - 4k > 0 \\Rightarrow 36 > 4k$\u3002",
      "$k < 9$\u3002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "level": 5,
    "topic": "Line-Curve Intersection",
    "question": "Find the coordinates of the points of intersection of the line $y = x + 1$ and the curve $y = x^2 - x - 2$.",
    "question_zh": "\u6c42\u76f4\u7dda $y = x + 1$ \u8207\u66f2\u7dda $y = x^2 - x - 2$ \u7684\u4ea4\u9ede\u5750\u6a19\u3002",
    "answer": "(-1, 0) and (3, 4)",
    "answer_zh": "(-1, 0) \u53ca (3, 4)",
    "steps": [
      "Equate the expressions: $x^2 - x - 2 = x + 1$.",
      "Rearrange to quadratic: $x^2 - 2x - 3 = 0$.",
      "Factorize: $(x - 3)(x + 1) = 0 \\Rightarrow x = 3$ or $x = -1$.",
      "Find corresponding $y$ values using line $y = x + 1$:",
      "For $x=3$, $y=4$. Intersection $(3, 4)$.",
      "For $x=-1$, $y=0$. Intersection $(-1, 0)$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "\u8a2d\u8868\u9054\u5f0f\u76f8\u7b49\uff1a$x^2 - x - 2 = x + 1$\u3002",
      "\u91cd\u6574\u70ba\u4e8c\u6b21\u65b9\u7a0b\uff1a$x^2 - 2x - 3 = 0$\u3002",
      "\u56e0\u5f0f\u5206\u89e3\uff1a$(x - 3)(x + 1) = 0 \\Rightarrow x = 3$ \u6216 $x = -1$\u3002",
      "\u5229\u7528\u76f4\u7dda $y = x + 1$ \u6c42\u76f8\u61c9\u7684 $y$ \u503c\uff1a",
      "\u7576 $x=3$ \u6642\uff0c$y=4$\u3002\u4ea4\u9ede\u70ba $(3, 4)$\u3002",
      "\u7576 $x=-1$ \u6642\uff0c$y=0$\u3002\u4ea4\u9ede\u70ba $(-1, 0)$\u3002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "level": 5,
    "topic": "Coordinate Geometry of Quadratics",
    "question": "Find the vertex and the axis of symmetry of $y = 2x^2 + 8x + 3$.",
    "question_zh": "\u6c42 $y = 2x^2 + 8x + 3$ \u7684\u9802\u9ede\u53ca\u5c0d\u7a31\u8ef8\u3002",
    "answer": "Vertex: (-2, -5), Axis: x = -2",
    "answer_zh": "\u9802\u9ede\uff1a(-2, -5)\uff0c\u5c0d\u7a31\u8ef8\uff1ax = -2",
    "steps": [
      "x-coordinate of vertex $h = -b/(2a) = -8/(2 \times 2) = -2$.",
      "y-coordinate $k = 2(-2)^2 + 8(-2) + 3 = 8 - 16 + 3 = -5$.",
      "Vertex is $(-2, -5)$.",
      "Axis of symmetry is $x = h$, so $x = -2$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "\u9802\u9ede\u7684 x \u5750\u6a19 $h = -b/(2a) = -8/(2 \times 2) = -2$\u3002",
      "y \u5750\u6a19 $k = 2(-2)^2 + 8(-2) + 3 = 8 - 16 + 3 = -5$\u3002",
      "\u9802\u9ede\u70ba $(-2, -5)$\u3002",
      "\u5c0d\u7a31\u8ef8\u70ba $x = h$\uff0c\u5373 $x = -2$\u3002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "level": 5,
    "topic": "Vieta's Formulas",
    "question": "If $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are the roots of $x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0$, evaluate $\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2$.",
    "question_zh": "\u82e5 $\\alpha$ \u53ca $\\beta$ \u70ba $x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0$ \u7684\u6839\uff0c\u6c42 $\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2$ \u7684\u503c\u3002",
    "answer": "14",
    "steps": [
      "From equation, $\\alpha + \\beta = 4$ and $\\alpha\\beta = 1$.",
      "$\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = (\\alpha + \\beta)^2 - 2\\alpha\\beta$.",
      "$\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = 4^2 - 2(1) = 16 - 2 = 14$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "\u6839\u64da\u65b9\u7a0b\uff0c$\\alpha + \\beta = 4$ \u4e14 $\\alpha\\beta = 1$\u3002",
      "$\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = (\\alpha + \\beta)^2 - 2\\alpha\\beta$\u3002",
      "$\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = 4^2 - 2(1) = 16 - 2 = 14$\u3002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "level": 5,
    "topic": "Root Transformations",
    "question": "The roots of $x^2 - 2x - 2 = 0$ are $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. Find a quadratic equation whose roots are $\\alpha+1$ and $\\beta+1$.",
    "question_zh": "$x^2 - 2x - 2 = 0$ \u7684\u6839\u70ba $\\alpha$ \u53ca $\\beta$\u3002\u6c42\u4e00\u500b\u4ee5 $\\alpha+1$ \u53ca $\\beta+1$ \u70ba\u6839\u7684\u4e8c\u6b21\u65b9\u7a0b\u3002",
    "answer": "x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0",
    "steps": [
      "Original: $\\alpha + \\beta = 2, \\alpha\\beta = -2$.",
      "New sum $S = (\\alpha+1) + (\\beta+1) = (\\alpha + \\beta) + 2 = 2 + 2 = 4$.",
      "New product $P = (\\alpha+1)(\\beta+1) = \\alpha\\beta + (\\alpha + \\beta) + 1 = -2 + 2 + 1 = 1$.",
      "New equation: $x^2 - Sx + P = 0 \\Rightarrow x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "\u539f\u65b9\u7a0b\uff1a$\\alpha + \\beta = 2, \\alpha\\beta = -2$\u3002",
      "\u65b0\u548c $S = (\\alpha+1) + (\\beta+1) = (\\alpha + \\beta) + 2 = 2 + 2 = 4$\u3002",
      "\u65b0\u7a4d $P = (\\alpha+1)(\\beta+1) = \\alpha\\beta + (\\alpha + \\beta) + 1 = -2 + 2 + 1 = 1$\u3002",
      "\u65b0\u65b9\u7a0b\uff1a$x^2 - Sx + P = 0 \\Rightarrow x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0$\u3002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "level": 5,
    "topic": "Line-Curve Intersection Condition",
    "question": "Find the range of $k$ such that the line $y = kx$ does not intersect the curve $y = x^2 + 1$.",
    "question_zh": "\u6c42 $k$ \u7684\u53d6\u503c\u7bc4\u570d\uff0c\u4f7f\u5f97\u76f4\u7dda $y = kx$ \u8207\u66f2\u7dda $y = x^2 + 1$ \u4e0d\u76f8\u4ea4\u3002",
    "answer": "-2 < k < 2",
    "steps": [
      "Equate: $x^2 + 1 = kx \\Rightarrow x^2 - kx + 1 = 0$.",
      "For no intersection, $\\Delta < 0$.",
      "$(-k)^2 - 4(1)(1) < 0 \\Rightarrow k^2 - 4 < 0$.",
      "$k^2 < 4 \\Rightarrow -2 < k < 2$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "\u8a2d\u76f8\u7b49\uff1a$x^2 + 1 = kx \\Rightarrow x^2 - kx + 1 = 0$\u3002",
      "\u5c0d\u65bc\u4e0d\u76f8\u4ea4\u72c0\u6cc1\uff0c$\\Delta < 0$\u3002",
      "$(-k)^2 - 4(1)(1) < 0 \\Rightarrow k^2 - 4 < 0$\u3002",
      "$k^2 < 4 \\Rightarrow -2 < k < 2$\u3002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "level": 5,
    "topic": "Line Tangent to Curve",
    "question": "The line $y = 2x + k$ is tangent to the curve $y = x^2 - 4x$. Find the value of $k$.",
    "question_zh": "\u76f4\u7dda $y = 2x + k$ \u662f\u66f2\u7dda $y = x^2 - 4x$ \u7684\u5207\u7dda\u3002\u6c42 $k$ \u7684\u503c\u3002",
    "answer": "-9",
    "steps": [
      "Equate expressions: $x^2 - 4x = 2x + k \\Rightarrow x^2 - 6x - k = 0$.",
      "Since it is tangent, $\\Delta = 0$.",
      "$(-6)^2 - 4(1)(-k) = 0$.",
      "$36 + 4k = 0 \\Rightarrow 4k = -36 \\Rightarrow k = -9$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "\u8a2d\u8868\u9054\u5f0f\u76f8\u7b49\uff1a$x^2 - 4x = 2x + k \\Rightarrow x^2 - 6x - k = 0$\u3002",
      "\u7531\u65bc\u662f\u76f8\u5207\uff0c$\\Delta = 0$\u3002",
      "$(-6)^2 - 4(1)(-k) = 0$\u3002",
      "$36 + 4k = 0 \\Rightarrow 4k = -36 \\Rightarrow k = -9$\u3002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "level": 5,
    "topic": "Properties of Function",
    "question": "Find the range of the function $f(x) = 2x^2 - 4x + 5$ for all real values of $x$.",
    "question_zh": "\u6c42\u51fd\u6578 $f(x) = 2x^2 - 4x + 5$ \u5c0d\u65bc\u6240\u6709 $x$ \u5be6\u6578\u503c\u7684\u5c0d\u61c9\u503c\u7bc4\u570d\uff08\u503c\u57df\uff09\u3002",
    "answer": "f(x) \\ge 3",
    "steps": [
      "Find the vertex: $x = -(-4)/(2 \times 2) = 1$.",
      "Minimum value $= f(1) = 2(1)^2 - 4(1) + 5 = 2 - 4 + 5 = 3$.",
      "Since $a = 2 > 0$, the parabola opens upwards.",
      "Range: $f(x) \\ge 3$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "\u6c42\u9802\u9ede\uff1a$x = -(-4)/(2 \times 2) = 1$\u3002",
      "\u6975\u5c0f\u503c $= f(1) = 2(1)^2 - 4(1) + 5 = 2 - 4 + 5 = 3$\u3002",
      "\u7531\u65bc $a = 2 > 0$\uff0c\u62cb\u7269\u7dda\u5411\u4e0a\u958b\u53e3\u3002",
      "\u503c\u57df\uff1a$f(x) \\ge 3$\u3002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "level": 5,
