    "question": "If $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are the roots of $2x^2 - 5x + 1 = 0$, evaluate $\\frac{1}{\\alpha^2} + \\frac{1}{\\beta^2}$.",
    "question_zh": "\u82e5 $\\alpha$ \u53ca $\\beta$ \u70ba $2x^2 - 5x + 1 = 0$ \u7684\u6839\uff0c\u6c42 $\\frac{1}{\\alpha^2} + \\frac{1}{\\beta^2}$ \u7684\u503c\u3002",
    "answer": "21",
    "steps": [
      "$\\alpha + \\beta = 2.5$, $\\alpha\\beta = 0.5$.",
      "$\\frac{1}{\\alpha^2} + \\frac{1}{\\beta^2} = \\frac{\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2}{(\\alpha\\beta)^2}$.",
      "$\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = (2.5)^2 - 2(0.5) = 6.25 - 1 = 5.25$.",
      "Result $= \\frac{5.25}{0.5^2} = \\frac{5.25}{0.25} = 21$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "$\\alpha + \\beta = 2.5$\uff0c$\\alpha\\beta = 0.5$\u3002",
      "$\\frac{1}{\\alpha^2} + \\frac{1}{\\beta^2} = \\frac{\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2}{(\\alpha\\beta)^2}$\u3002",
      "$\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = (2.5)^2 - 2(0.5) = 6.25 - 1 = 5.25$\u3002",
      "\u7d50\u679c $= \\frac{5.25}{0.5^2} = \\frac{5.25}{0.25} = 21$\u3002"
    ]
  },
