    "question": "The roots of $x^2 - 4x + 2 = 0$ are $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. Form a quadratic equation whose roots are $\\alpha^2$ and $\\beta^2$.",
    "question_zh": "$x^2 - 4x + 2 = 0$ \u7684\u6839\u70ba $\\alpha$ \u53ca $\\beta$\u3002\u6c42\u4e00\u500b\u4ee5 $\\alpha^2$ \u53ca $\\beta^2$ \u70ba\u6839\u7684\u4e8c\u6b21\u65b9\u7a0b\u3002",
    "answer": "x^2 - 12x + 4 = 0",
    "steps": [
      "$\\alpha + \\beta = 4, \\alpha\\beta = 2$.",
      "New sum $S = \\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = (\\alpha + \\beta)^2 - 2\\alpha\\beta = 4^2 - 2(2) = 12$.",
      "New product $P = \\alpha^2\\beta^2 = (\\alpha\\beta)^2 = 2^2 = 4$.",
      "New equation: $x^2 - Sx + P = 0 \\Rightarrow x^2 - 12x + 4 = 0$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "$\\alpha + \\beta = 4, \\alpha\\beta = 2$\u3002",
      "\u65b0\u548c $S = \\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = (\\alpha + \\beta)^2 - 2\\alpha\\beta = 4^2 - 2(2) = 12$\u3002",
      "\u65b0\u7a4d $P = \\alpha^2\\beta^2 = (\\alpha\\beta)^2 = 2^2 = 4$\u3002",
      "\u65b0\u65b9\u7a0b\uff1a$x^2 - Sx + P = 0 \\Rightarrow x^2 - 12x + 4 = 0$\u3002"
    ]
  },
