    "level": 7,
    "topic": "Advanced Discriminant",
    "question": "For what values of $k$ does the equation $x^2 + (k-2)x + (k+1) = 0$ have real roots?",
    "question_zh": "\u7576 $k$ \u53d6\u4f55\u503c\u6642\uff0c\u65b9\u7a0b $x^2 + (k-2)x + (k+1) = 0$ \u6709\u5be6\u6839\uff1f",
    "answer": "k \\le 0 or k \\ge 8",
    "steps": [
      "For real roots, $\\Delta \\ge 0$.",
      "$(k-2)^2 - 4(1)(k+1) \\ge 0$.",
      "$k^2 - 4k + 4 - 4k - 4 \\ge 0$.",
      "$k^2 - 8k \\ge 0 \\Rightarrow k(k - 8) \\ge 0$.",
      "$k \\le 0$ or $k \\ge 8$."
    ],
    "steps_zh": [
      "\u5c0d\u65bc\u5be6\u6839\uff0c$\\Delta \\ge 0$\u3002",
      "$(k-2)^2 - 4(1)(k+1) \\ge 0$\u3002",
      "$k^2 - 4k + 4 - 4k - 4 \\ge 0$\u3002",
      "$k^2 - 8k \\ge 0 \\Rightarrow k(k - 8) \\ge 0$\u3002",
      "$k \\le 0$ \u6216 $k \\ge 8$\u3002"
    ]
  }
]
